quence, and N4 is terminal.\n  - Therefore, Player 1 can win immediately by moving to N7 and then to N4.\n\nWait — the rules say: players alternate moving a token along one directed edge. A player with no legal move loses.\n\nSo Player 1 starts at N3. They make the first move.\n\nIf Player 1 moves from N3 to N7, then it's Player 2's turn at N7.\n\nPlayer 2 must now move from N7 to N4, N0, or N5.\n\n- If Player 2 moves to N4 → terminal → Player 2 wins.\n- If Player 2 moves to N0 → then Player 1 can go to N6, and so on.\n- If Player 2 moves to N5 → then Player 1 can go to N1 or N2, both terminal → Player 1 wins.\n\nSo if Player 2 moves to N5, Player 1 can win immediately.\n\nIf Player 2 moves to N0, then Player 1 can go to N6, and from N6, Player 2 can go to N8 or N9, both terminal — so Player 2 wins.\n\nSo from N7, Player 2 has choices:\n- To N4 → wins immediately.\n- To N0 → Player 1 goes to N6 → Player 2 goes to N8 or N9 → wins.\n- To N5 → Player 1 goes to N1 or N2 → both terminal → Player 1 wins.\n\nSo if Player 2 moves to N5, Player 1 wins. If Player 2 moves to N4 or N0, Player 2 wins.\n\nSo Player 2 will choose the winning move — either N4 or N0 — and win.\n\nTherefore, if Player 1 moves to N7, Player 2 can win by moving to N4 or N0.\n\nSo Player 1 cannot win immediately from N7.\n\nBut wait — is there a move from N3 that leads to a winning position?\n\nWait — what if Player 1 moves to N0?\n\nThen Player 2 is at N0 → must go to N6.\n\nThen Player 2 moves to N6 → can go to N8 or N9.\n\n- N8 → terminal → Player 2 wins.\n- N9 → from N9, can go to N8 or N2 → both terminal → so Player 2 can move to either and win.\n\nSo again, Player 2 wins.\n\nSo both N0 and N7 lead to Player 2 winning?\n\nBut earlier I thought from N7 → N4 is terminal — but that's a move by the player at N7.\n\nPlayer 1 starts at N3.\n\nIf Player 1 moves to N7, then it's Player 2's turn at N7.\n\nPlayer 2 must move from N7.\n\nPlayer 2 can go to:\n- N4 → terminal → Player 2 wins.\n- N0 → then Playe